Fix CSV import: model has no 'expenses' column — every row failed

The import-csv handler passed expenses= to FinancialRecord, which has
cogs/opex/other_costs instead — SQLAlchemy raised on every row, so every
CSV import ever attempted wrote 0 records while the toast said 'Import
successful'. Found live during the founder role-play test.

- store the mapped Expenses column as opex; add cogs/other_costs to
  detection and import so full P&L CSVs keep their cost split
- net burn now sums all present cost components minus revenue; gross
  margin computed from revenue/cogs when not supplied
- skip rows with unparseable dates instead of failing the whole commit
  (period columns are non-nullable)
- toast is now honest: destructive 'Import failed' at 0 rows, partial
  count otherwise; 'Upload Financials' empty-state CTA now goes to
  /data-input instead of bouncing off completed onboarding

